<id>https://music.hugofloresgarcia.art/world-of-mouth-binaural-version/</id>
<link href="https://music.hugofloresgarcia.art/world-of-mouth-binaural-version/" rel="alternate"/>
<summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;world of mouth is a fixed media 8-channel composition for a generative sound neural network and voice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In world of mouth, I construct several sonic environments entirely out of gestures recorded with my own voice. These vocal gestures are used as guidance for a generative model trained on a sound library of percussion instruments and natural sounds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The vocal gestures gave timbral and rhythmic shape to the generated sounds, which contain the sonic properties of the collected material (e.g. percussion + natural sounds), while still following the patterns of my voice. The result is a fascinating morphing process between sound textures: we can listen my vocal gesture give shape to the sound material, but eventually, the sound material bites back, imposing its own rhythmic properties into the resulting sound.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you would like a copy of the 8-channel version, email me hugggofloresgarcia [at] gmail [dot] com.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;premiered at Experimental Sound Studio (ess.org) in Chicago, IL on Feb 25th, 2024.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-- the mouth is the interface --&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This piece is a result of my research work in generative modelling for sound (i.e. vampnet). Vampnet allows me to collect a large amount of sound material and converts it from a static sound into a malleable set of sound objects. With the model, I can mold and give shape to the sound materials I collected by way of other sonic gestures, like those that I can imitate with my mouth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So for word of mouth, I collected natural and percussion sounds, trained a vampnet model of these sounds, and performed a set of gestures with my voice to guide the model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The implications of this voice-&amp;gt;generative model technique from a sound sculpting perspective are incredibly intriguing, and I hope this piece inspires people to try this technique in their own creative practice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="divider"&gt;
    &lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;note: this is a binaural version of a work originally composed for an octophonic speaker system (four stereo pairs laid out in an octagon). for a better spatial experience, &lt;strong&gt;headphones are recommended&lt;/strong&gt;. If you would like a copy of the 8-channel version, email me hugggofloresgarcia [at] gmail [dot] com.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;composed and performed by Hugo Flores García.
album artwork by Camilla Forte.
special thanks to Chris Mercer for his guidance and advice while composing for an 8-channel loudspeaker system.&lt;/p&gt;
</summary>
<title>hugo flores garcía – world of mouth (binaural version)</title>
<updated>2026-10-25T17:57:09.044639+00:00</updated></entry>
